<section class="space-y-4">
    <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">Why we hold it</h2>
    <dl class="space-y-3 text-content-muted leading-relaxed">
        <div>
            <dt class="font-medium text-content">To carry out a contract with you</dt>
            <dd>Delivering the build for a client, engaging a subcontractor or supplier, paying an
                operative for their time, and running your portal account.</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
            <dt class="font-medium text-content">Because the law requires it</dt>
            <dd>Construction Industry Scheme returns, tax and accounting records, health and safety
                records, and building control submissions.</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
            <dt class="font-medium text-content">In our legitimate interests as a business</dt>
            <dd>Running projects to time and budget, keeping an audit trail of who did what, keeping the
                portal secure, answering an enquiry you made, and measuring the service we give our clients.
                We weigh these against your interests and stop where yours outweigh ours.</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
            <dt class="font-medium text-content">With your consent</dt>
            <dd>Keeping in touch about your home after we have sent you your concepts. You choose this
                separately on the imagine page and can withdraw it there at any time.</dd>
        </div>
    </dl>
</section>

<section class="space-y-4">
    <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">Who handles it for us, and where</h2>
    <p class="text-content-muted leading-relaxed">
        The portal runs on Microsoft Azure in the European Economic Area (Ireland and the Netherlands),
        which the UK recognises as offering adequate protection. We use these services, each under a
        contract that limits them to working on our instructions:
    </p>
    <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1 text-content-muted leading-relaxed">
        <li><span class="text-content">Microsoft</span> — hosting, the projects mailbox (Microsoft 365), the
            emails the portal sends, text recognition on scanned documents, and the concept pictures made
            from photographs of your home.</li>
        <li><span class="text-content">Anthropic</span> — the assistant our staff use to read and summarise
            correspondence, drawings and documents. It works on what our staff ask it to read and is not
            used to train its models.</li>
        <li><span class="text-content">Xero</span> — our accounts: invoices, bills, payments and the
            contact details they carry.</li>
        <li><span class="text-content">Bluebeam Studio</span> (UK) — reading dimensions and notes off
            architects' drawings.</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="text-content-muted leading-relaxed">
        Beyond these we share your details only where the project needs it — a client's architect
        sees the requests and variations on their project; a subcontractor sees the orders placed with
        them — and where the law requires it, such as HMRC for CIS. We never sell your details.
    </p>
</section>
